A wand of Wishing should immediately change your game play. It is not
always
that you get an early wish and you should become focused on winning the
game,
rather than surviving. This involves using your wishes to improve your
character
enough to make your game easy, and then leveling up fast. But that
doesn't mean
you can play fast and reckless.

I would never wish for a GDSM if I know that I have one more pending
wish.

MR is more important than Reflection but MR is necessary only after
Oracle,
when polymorph traps start to occur. Also Polytraps are dangerous but
they
can be survived most of the time, if you have buff pets. You may lose
your
cloak if wearing SDSM but that is not too much of a problem as
replacements
can be found easily.

It is better to get a Quest Artifacts of other characters for MR as
they don't use any slots,
EoA (for neutral spellcasters),  PYEC or EoO (for other neutrals), and
SoM(for lawfuls).
IMO PYEC is slightly better for characters that can't cast +DM at
skilled or better levels,
as it gives telepathy without using a slot.
It is better to get reflection from SDSM as it saves the amulet slot.

So the general strategy is to wish for SDSM and then increase your HP
above 40
by leveling up, then wish for an MR granting Quest Artifact.

Other wishes depend on situation and character. Magic whistles are very
useful for
a healer, but its not an absolute necessity. Also they are frequently
found in the Dungeon.

